Scope: Oracle #327 plus explicit private-HOME guard b4760d4a and append-only night/quarantine scope88238bb6. This is an incremental cut, NOT completion of the full sweep. Baseline inventory385 cases,383 reviewed; the two unreviewed cases and peer-owned gui_events/native_keychain/identity files are excluded. #326 remains pending; no invariant activation is made.

Mechanisms:
- Add294 keeps tags, while preserving29 existing tags;19 tag candidates across3 peer-owned files deliberately untouched. References are checked against repository specs/invariants; comments are in tests or cfg(test) modules.
- Provider GUI parents use an owned subprocess with env_clear, private HOME/ZDOTDIR and memory custody. GUI Update/Applied conditions replace Snapshot text polls, a received notification advances fake RTT, and provider drop/reconnect phases are explicit. Restart links are made Connected before the readiness boundary. Three exact original parent names are appended to night-test-boundaries.sh, no blanket ignored run.
- The installed-client driver refuses before spawn unless Command HOME names its owned TempDir. Both inherited and foreign HOME are denied by PermissionDenied. No operator config/key is read or copied. Real installed clients under a private HOME need a test credential: UNPROVEN and not run.
- Knowledge tests compare portable DTOs, filtered graphs/briefs/pages and typed refusals; unexposed/forbidden provider methods panic. GUI scheduler tests compare actual iteration order/exhaustion and emitted Update sequences. A newer Update remains gated after duplicate/wrong ACK and is released only by its exact Applied. Typed InvalidData refusals replace incidental writer/schema English; original file bytes/data and schema markers remain unchanged.
- Native custody controls must complete while the injected backend remains held. The500ms wall-clock assertion is removed. Entry is a mutex/Condvar rendezvous; retained result/audit checks are woken by private SQLite vnode changes on macOS. Read-only kqueue registration uses120s hangguards, no sleeps/polls. Non-macOS fixture fallback is unvalidated here. The backend is synthetic; no login Keychain/native credential access occurs.
- The only production change is a private idle-policy clock seam: Policy::idle_due(arrived, now) replaces the same elapsed-time comparison at its original call site. A199/200ms boundary and later-byte reset test replaces the defaults snapshot. R/2R, K=4,60s age, forced saves and all durability paths remain unchanged.

