- A2 fixture_drains_notifications_while_waiting_and_keeps_a_split_reply: deleted; actual provider GUI routing/reconnect/restart boundary still exercises those fixture readers against production.
- A2 a_refusal_queued_before_the_request_survives_a_broken_pipe: deleted; ctl_endpoint_opt_in_and_ancestry_refusal still drives the real production door, and seat_socket::gui_tests::refusal_drains_the_complete_request_before_half_closing retains refusal/EOF coverage.
- A3 checkpoint::tests::policy_is_data_with_the_decided_budgets: replaced by idle_checkpoint_requires_two_hundred_milliseconds_since_the_last_arrival. Other behavior tests retain R-spaced recovery, K occupancy and60s oldest-byte age.

