The9 paths are tests/common/record_supervisor.rs, tests/mcp.rs, cfg(test) modules in src/{gui_capture,ctl_door,mcp/journal}.rs, tests/{provider,provider_fake,test_account}.rs, and append-only scripts/night-test-boundaries.sh. Production prefixes in all3 source modules compare byte-for-byte equal to their parent; mcp-cut-final-prefix-proof.json records that proof.
Record/authority tests retain real Logic, SQLite, signing and admitted MCP bridge while using an empty-capture SupervisorConnection. No shell is launched for each of the4 base seats. Unexpected terminal effects panic. Input/capture/spawn/native paths explicitly select the real Supervisor. The installed-client guard still rejects inherited/foreign HOME before spawn. No operator identity, native Keychain or real credential was accessed.
Five original parent selectors are appended to the night script: mcp_seat_input_consumes_readiness_and_enter_is_explicit, mcp_seat_input_lost_receipt_is_unknown_and_never_repeated_after_restart, mcp_seat_reads_page_real_capture_and_refuse_stale_view_cursors, mcp_seat_spawn_runs_once_with_isolated_home_and_existing_wiring, mcp_seat_native_interrupt_is_bounded_audited_and_never_replayed. Each was executed separately via its exact --ignored --exact command and passed. No blanket ignored run.
Lost-receipt readiness now uses the one-shot shell and observed ready state instead of80ms or0.6s timed rearm. Native automatic-reader installation is established by the first actual read-only thread/read request.8 held native operations remain pending before and after concurrent controls, replacing the1500ms speed assertion. The product2s native deadline is unchanged. Owned child completion uses Tokio child.wait and bounded pipe readers, replacing10/20ms try_wait loops; private config and owned process-group cleanup retained.
GUI capture/window tests directly poll futures under paused Tokio time. Wrong operation replies remain Pending; exact replies complete; serial same-id reuse proves admission release. Tests assert public frame/notice/refusal results rather than private maps, incidental product English or task scheduling. ctl ancestry uses the existing classify_with seam; actual endpoint/ancestry coverage remains. Journal2-caller Barrier and exact committed outcome/effect-count/audit assertions retain concurrency proof without30ms scheduler encouragement.
Routing tests compare distinct per-host returned SeatInfo markers instead of private mock request vectors; explicit local-blocking/remote-zero-wait policy remains. Missing/corrupt/foreign account and mixed-host batch checks use InvalidData while retaining no-effect/original-byte assertions.
Failure retained: first record-supervisor attempt used pid0, which real attachment validation rejects (invalid harness attachment identity).43 MCP failures shared that setup cause; lib/provider/fake/account passed. The fixture now identifies its own hosting test PID; no child is created, and product validation is unchanged. Subsequent MCP45/0, then the full crate352/0. Failed and passing output remains separately hashed.

Prechecks bind their recorded HEAD plus WIP diff hash. Subsequent rustfmt changed test formatting only; it briefly touched one pre-existing production formatting block, restored byte-for-byte before commit. The exact signed/rebased source is checked again by land.sh. No precheck is claimed to run on an unstated clean SHA.
