# NUM2 fixture race: natural failure, forced counterexample and isolated-input fix

The second MCP author attempt failed one real test: mcp_artifact_number_uses_unindexed_records_of_every_type_and_keeps_retry_bytes expected9002 but received9003. The test created a numbered spec under the live provenance watcher, which legitimately allocated the next artifact number before the explicit claim. Detector::new registers the primary repository; the detector includes that nested path, and materialization allocates through Index. A temporary test-only notification observer waited for the real competing9002 artifact and reproduced9003 versus9002 (EXIT101). All diagnostic hooks were restored byte for byte before the permanent fixture change.
